    "result_text": "The full build passes. There's only one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and it passes along with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` as specified.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 reworked `nextCustomerCode`:\n- Now takes both `city` and `lastName`.\n- `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the city; `LAST3` = upper-cased first three of the last name.\n- `NNNN` is now a **per-city** 4-digit zero-padded sequence \u2014 one more than the number of owners already in that city (previously a global count), computed by filtering `findAllOwners()` on city (case-insensitive, matching the existing `equalsIgnoreCase` helper).\n- Updated the call site and javadoc accordingly.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `membershipNumber` (formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`) reads `owner.getCustomerCode()` directly, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format; I only refreshed its javadoc example (`MEL-SMI-0007-M26`) to match.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix`, which asserts the code matches `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`, passes.",
